    For complex-valued inputs:

    >>> x1 = jnp.array([4-3j, 2j])
    >>> with jnp.printoptions(precision=3, suppress=True):
    ...   jnp.arcsinh(x1)
    Array([2.306-0.634j, 1.317+1.571j], dtype=complex64)

